l0-static-graph: a fix to intel/llvm v7.2.0, applied by tools/intel_llvm_build.py.

Where the system's Level Zero is older than 1.32 (Ubuntu 26.04's libze 1.28, where the packages are
built), the Level Zero adapters link the loader statically, and the static loader forwards the stable
record and replay graph functions to the system's loader at run time.  The system's 1.28 loader lacks
them, and the static one then answers the first call UNSUPPORTED and calls a null pointer on the next
(the static loader's ze_libapi.cpp, 1.32 to 1.34).  The adapter took the functions as there, the
static loader's own entry points being not null, whenever the driver announced the stable graph
extension: compute-runtime 26.35.39758.10 does.  handler::finalize asks every queue whether a graph
capture is on, and oneMKL's GEMM submits through the handler, so the engine ended with SIGSEGV at its
first product with oneMKL installed on an Arc Pro B70 (XeStrata issue #12).  Fixed, with the static
loader the graph functions are used only when the system's loader has them, as the static one finds
them (libze_loader.so.1, ze_loader.dll).
---
diff --git a/unified-runtime/source/adapters/level_zero/platform.cpp b/unified-runtime/source/adapters/level_zero/platform.cpp
index 0550345b8b..1c3c4dd3ce 100644
--- a/unified-runtime/source/adapters/level_zero/platform.cpp
+++ b/unified-runtime/source/adapters/level_zero/platform.cpp
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 // Part of the LLVM Project, under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM
 // Exceptions. See https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt for license information.
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
+// Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: the static loader's graph functions only when the system's loader has them (l0-static-graph)
 //
 //===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
 
@@ -768,6 +769,42 @@ ur_result_t ur_platform_handle_t_::initialize() {
           (ZeGraphExt.zeGraphDumpContentsExp != nullptr) &&
           (ZeGraphExt.zeGraphDestroyExp != nullptr) &&
           (ZeGraphExt.zeExecutableGraphDestroyExp != nullptr);
+#ifdef UR_STATIC_LEVEL_ZERO
+      // The statically linked loader forwards these entry points to the
+      // system's Level Zero loader, which may predate them (1.28): the static
+      // one then answers the first call UNSUPPORTED and calls a null pointer
+      // on the next (its ze_libapi.cpp, loader 1.32 to 1.34).  A driver that
+      // announces the stable graph extension (compute-runtime 26.35) with such
+      // a loader ended the program at its second graph-capture query.  So they
+      // are used only when the system's loader has them.
+      {
+#ifdef _WIN32
+        auto SystemLoader =
+            ur_loader::LibLoader::loadAdapterLibrary("ze_loader.dll");
+#else
+        auto SystemLoader =
+            ur_loader::LibLoader::loadAdapterLibrary("libze_loader.so.1");
+#endif
+        auto Has = [&](const char *Name) {
+          return SystemLoader &&
+                 ur_loader::LibLoader::getFunctionPtr(SystemLoader.get(),
+                                                      Name) != nullptr;
+        };
+        for (const char *Name :
+             {"zeCommandListBeginGraphCaptureExt",
+              "zeCommandListBeginCaptureIntoGraphExt",
+              "zeCommandListEndGraphCaptureExt", "zeCommandListAppendGraphExt",
+              "zeCommandListIsGraphCaptureEnabledExt", "zeGraphCreateExt",
+              "zeGraphInstantiateExt", "zeGraphIsEmptyExt",
+              "zeGraphDumpContentsExt", "zeGraphDestroyExt",
+              "zeExecutableGraphDestroyExt"})
+          ZeGraphExt.Supported = ZeGraphExt.Supported && Has(Name);
+        if (!Has("zeCommandListGetGraphExt"))
+          ZeGraphExt.zeCommandListGetGraphExp = nullptr;
+        if (!Has("zeGraphSetDestructionCallbackExt"))
+          ZeGraphExt.zeGraphSetDestructionCallbackExp = nullptr;
+      }
+#endif
     }
 
     // zeGraphGetIdExt must be special-cased: it isn't part of the graph DDI
